firing-log

Record of every engine firing on the test stand: date, engine, seconds, thrust, result, operator, note.

Rows are plain text, one per firing, appended by the operator at the console. `flog grid` prints the
year as a grid so the stand crew can see how a campaign is actually going, not how it is reported.

Build

  go build ./...

Usage

  flog add -engine merlin1c -seconds 30 -thrust 340 -result ok
  flog grid -year 2010

Columns

  date, engine, seconds, thrust_kn, result, operator, note

result is one of ok, aborted, RUD. Anything else is a typo and the parser rejects the row.

Adding a firing

Append only. Do not edit a row after the shift ends. Corrections go in note.

Layout

  log/firings.csv   the log, one row per firing
  grid/             year grid renderer
  add.go            appends a row, validates columns
- columns: date, engine, seconds, thrust, result, operator, note
- note: do not edit rows after the shift
- layout section
- build section
